Wine starts every Windows program from the loader inside the engine's mavrik.app, so macOS can give a full-screen game Game Mode.

This repository's patch (version 3), after neutron's two hunks: fourlexboehm/neutron at 0ac2574d, wine patches 0003
(ntdll execs the bundled loader) and 0006 (the loader finds ntdll.so from inside the bundle), by the neutron
contributors, LGPL-2.1-or-later. neutron names its
bundle Neutron.app and also takes a per-game bundle from NEUTRON_APP_BUNDLE and NEUTRON_NTDLL; this patch keeps only
the one shared bundle, so nothing is made at run time.

macOS gives Game Mode to a game in full screen, and it knows an app is a game that supports Game Mode from its
bundle's Info.plist (LSApplicationCategoryType public.app-category.games and LSSupportsGameMode, with
GCSupportsGameMode for macOS 14 to 25). A bundle's Info.plist applies to the executable at
Contents/MacOS/<CFBundleExecutable>. Wine's loader is a bare executable, and version 1 of this patch put the keys in
its embedded Info.plist (__TEXT,__info_plist): macOS ignored them (the Metal HUD read Game Mode Off and gamepolicyd
logged nothing, in Wine's full screen and in a full-screen Space, mavrik S217). A lab bundle around the loader got
Game Mode On in both (gamepolicyd: "Found game ... labelReason=LSSupportsGameMode (Info.plist)", then "Game mode
enabled.").

The engine's recipe (scripts/assemble.py) lays lib/wine/x86_64-unix/mavrik.app/Contents/{Info.plist, MacOS/wine},
the second a copy of the loader, and signs it as a bundle. Beside it, lib/wine/x86_64-unix/without-game-mode/
mavrik.app is the same bundle without the three Game Mode keys and with its own identifier
(org.mavrik.engine.wine.without-game-mode), for a player who turns Game Mode off for a game (version 3). This patch:
- dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c, init_paths: wineloader, the file every Windows program is exec'd from, becomes
  <ntdll_dir>/mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS/wine when that file is executable; otherwise it stays <ntdll_dir>/wine, as
  before. With MAVRIK_GAME_MODE=0 in the environment (exactly "0"; any other value or none keeps Game Mode) it is
  <ntdll_dir>/without-game-mode/mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS/wine instead, or <ntdll_dir>/wine without that bundle, so
  "off" never gives Game Mode. Wine passes the variable to every process the program starts, as it passes
  WINEPRELOADERAPPNAME, so a launcher's game follows it. Both bundles have the same folder name, so macOS's Local
  Network prompt reads "mavrik" for either, and the same CFBundleName, so a program started with no link reads
  "mavrik" either way. Patch 0007's link named after the game is made to wineloader, so it now points into the bundle: the window
  server keeps the link's name, and the kernel runs the bundle's file, whose bundle macOS reads.
- dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c, create_tempdir (CW HACK 22144): the folder's ntdll.so link points at ntdll.so, three
  folders up from the bundle's loader (four from the one without Game Mode), not at a file beside it that does not
  exist. Each loader has its own link folder (the folder is named after the loader's inode), so a game's link
  carries its name in both states.
- loader/main.c, try_dlopen: a loader running from mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS finds ntdll.so three folders up (four
  from without-game-mode/mavrik.app), as one in loader/ finds it in the build tree.

Why a second bundle and not the bare loader for "off" (version 3): the bare loader differs from the bundle in more
than Game Mode. A program started from it with no link reads "wine" in the menu bar, and the process has another
identity for macOS (activation and the Local Network prompt). The second bundle changes only the Game Mode keys, so
turning Game Mode off changes only Game Mode, and measuring on against off measures Game Mode alone.

Version 1's three keys in loader/wine_info.plist.in are gone: they did nothing, and the bundle's Info.plist holds
them now.

Upstream status: mavrik's own layout (the bundle's name and place are this engine's), not offered. A WineHQ offer
would need a configurable bundle; the Game Mode finding is offered as a note with the engine's other upstream offers.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index b336af3..a3bffc8 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -185,6 +185,13 @@
 static const char *bin_dir;
 static const char *dll_dir;
 static const char *ntdll_dir;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/* mavrik: the folders, below ntdll_dir, of the loaders inside the engine's two app bundles:
+ * mavrik.app declares a game that supports Game Mode; without-game-mode/mavrik.app is the
+ * same bundle without those keys, used when MAVRIK_GAME_MODE is "0" */
+#define MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE "mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS"
+#define MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE_NO_GAME_MODE "without-game-mode/" MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE
+#endif
 static const char *alt_build_dir;
 static SIZE_T dll_path_maxlen;
 
@@ -500,6 +507,26 @@
         bin_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", BINDIR );
         data_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", DATADIR "/wine" );
         wineloader = build_path( ntdll_dir, "wine" );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        /* mavrik, after neutron: start every Windows program from the loader inside
+         * the engine's mavrik.app bundle, so macOS reads that bundle's Info.plist
+         * (a game that supports Game Mode).  The loader there finds ntdll.so through
+         * its real path; without the bundle, the loader beside ntdll.so is used.
+         * MAVRIK_GAME_MODE=0 picks the bundle without the Game Mode keys instead; every
+         * process the program starts keeps the variable, so its children follow it. */
+        {
+            const char *game_mode = getenv( "MAVRIK_GAME_MODE" );
+            char *bundled = build_path( ntdll_dir, game_mode && !strcmp( game_mode, "0" )
+                                        ? MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE_NO_GAME_MODE "/wine"
+                                        : MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE "/wine" );
+            if (!access( bundled, X_OK ))
+            {
+                free( (char *)wineloader );
+                wineloader = bundled;
+            }
+            else free( bundled );
+        }
+#endif
     }
 
     set_dll_path();
@@ -731,6 +758,14 @@
     ntdll = malloc( strlen(wineloader_path) + sizeof("/ntdll.so") );
     strcpy( ntdll, wineloader_path );
     if ((p = strrchr( ntdll, '/' ))) *p = 0;
+    /* mavrik: the loader inside mavrik.app has ntdll.so three folders up, and the one
+     * inside without-game-mode/mavrik.app four */
+    if ((p = remove_tail( ntdll, "/" MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE_NO_GAME_MODE )) ||
+        (p = remove_tail( ntdll, "/" MAVRIK_LOADER_BUNDLE )))
+    {
+        strcpy( ntdll, p );
+        free( p );
+    }
     strcat( ntdll, "/ntdll.so" );
     asprintf( &str, "%s/ntdll.so", tempdir );
     symlink( ntdll, str );
diff --git a/loader/main.c b/loader/main.c
index 6b21fe6..7ed8052 100644
--- a/loader/main.c
+++ b/loader/main.c
@@ -166,6 +166,11 @@
 
     if ((p = remove_tail( dir, "/loader" )))
         path = build_path( p, "dlls/ntdll/ntdll.so" );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    else if ((p = remove_tail( dir, "/without-game-mode/mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS" )) ||
+             (p = remove_tail( dir, "/mavrik.app/Contents/MacOS" )))
+        path = build_path( p, "ntdll.so" );  /* mavrik, after neutron: the loader inside one of the engine's app bundles */
+#endif
     else
         path = build_path( dir, "ntdll.so" );
 
